  "headline": "Mirissa & Weligama: Azure Bays, Stilt Fishermen & the Blue Whale Highway",
  "description": "Off Mirissa the continental shelf drops away close to shore, bringing blue whales, sperm whales and spinner dolphins within reach of a morning boat trip. Along the bays, stilt fishermen still perch above the surf and Weligama’s gentle waves make it the island’s classic place to learn to surf.\n\nI book small, licensed vessels that respect distance rules and pair the ocean days with quiet beach villas, coconut-cliff sunsets and slow seafood dinners.",
